Campfire wasm patch 0107: Rescan.

A wallet restored from its 12 words finds its coins by reading BEAM's
recovery snapshot once, then the blocks after it. When a balance is still
wrong (the snapshot was skipped or interrupted, or another copy of the seed
spent coins while this wallet was not reading blocks), BEAM's wallets offer
Rescan: Wallet::Rescan forgets every coin, except those a transaction under
way is creating, and finds them again from the blockchain. Without an owned
node that means reading every block since genesis, an hour or more in a
browser, and the wasm client did not expose it at all.

This adds WasmWalletClient.setRescan(bool), called before startWallet()
together with importRecovery/importRecoveryFromFile. The snapshot import
then runs as WalletDB::RescanFromRecovery: the coins and shielded coins are
forgotten (those created by pending, in-progress or registering
transactions are kept, as Wallet::Rescan keeps them), the stored UTXO events
are dropped, and the snapshot is imported, all in one database transaction.
If the snapshot cannot be read, the transaction is rolled back and the
wallet is exactly as it was. Transaction history and addresses are kept.

